<title>EGYPT: Italy's Enel takes 25,000 t/month Egyptian fuel oi.</title>
<headline>Italy's Enel takes 25,000 t/month Egyptian fuel oi.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian state power company Enel contracted to buy 25,000 tonnes a month of Egyptian low sulphur fuel oil throughout 1997 at Platts FOB Med mean +$7.76 a tonne, a source close to the deal said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>State-owned Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) has now awarded contracts for all its low sulphur fuel oil through 1997, the source said. BP has contracted to buy 50,000 tonnes a month, at the same price as Enel.</p>
<p>Enel took most of EGPC's fuel oil this year, the source said.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
